The duties of the city clerk shall be to:
(1) Attend, in person, all sessions of the municipal court, and keep a correct record of all monies collected by police officers for fines and those turned over to the city clerk;
(2) Keep all of the city books;
(3) Attend to all the correspondence of the city;
(4) Attend, in person, all meetings of the board of council, and keep correct minutes of the proceedings;
(5) Collect all taxes, with the help of police officers, and keep a correct record of such taxes collected;
(6) Help collect all utility bills due the city, with the help and assistance of the heads of the water and gas departments, and keep a correct record of such collections;
(7) Devote himself at such hours as prescribed by the board of council to the city's business, as required by laws and ordinances;
(8) Keep the city's books, papers and records so free and easy access can be had to such books, papers and records by the board of council and other officials of the city;
(9) Perform all of the duties of the city clerk as required by the board of council, as such duties appear in the laws affecting the city, of this Code and in the ordinances of the city; and
(10) Give a performance bond in such amount as required by the board of council.
(Code 1982, § 2-4-2)

